    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Cleaning decisions\n",
        "\n",
        "The final-grade histogram shows a spike at G3 = 0. Students with G3 = 0 have exactly 0 recorded absences and declining earlier grades, which suggests they did not complete the course. I exclude them (n = 38), so the analysis covers students who sat the final exam (n = 357).\n",
        "\n",
        "G1 and G2 (earlier grades) are also excluded from the features because they almost determine G3 (data leakage). The goal is to understand background and behavior, not to repeat last term's grade."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IQ0YhNFTozSH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Look at the zero-grade group\n",
        "sns.histplot(df[\"G3\"], bins=11, kde=True)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribution of final math grades (G3)\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Final grade (G3)\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Number of students\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "is_zero = df[\"G3\"] == 0\n",
        "print(is_zero.value_counts())\n",
        "print(df.groupby(is_zero)[[\"absences\", \"failures\", \"studytime\", \"G1\", \"G2\"]].mean())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JwzraYhyoevD",
        "outputId": "06cb9e24-6af4-4e27-fc69-5dcbd4026922",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 619
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "G3\n",
            "False    357\n",
            "True      38\n",
            "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
            "       absences  failures  studytime         G1         G2\n",
            "G3                                                        \n",
            "False  6.316527  0.271709   2.042017  11.268908  11.358543\n",
            "True   0.000000  0.921053   1.973684   7.526316   4.657895\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Keep students who sat the final exam, then create the pass/fail target\n",
        "df_clean = df[df[\"G3\"] > 0].copy()\n",
        "df_clean[\"pass\"] = (df_clean[\"G3\"] >= 10).astype(int)  # 1 = pass, 0 = fail\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Clean shape:\", df_clean.shape)\n",
        "print(df_clean[\"pass\"].value_counts())\n",
        "print(df_clean[\"pass\"].value_counts(normalize=True).round(3))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BmS4nNDLo-8I",
        "outputId": "c713eaa9-1beb-4fc6-a036-f24b2512e926",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Clean shape: (357, 34)\n",
            "pass\n",
            "1    265\n",
            "0     92\n",
            "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
            "pass\n",
            "1    0.742\n",
            "0    0.258\n",
            "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cgHnb5txvE4h"
      },
      "source": [
        "**What this shows.** The 38 students with G3 = 0 have exactly 0 recorded absences, more past failures (0.92 vs 0.27) and falling earlier grades (mean G2 of 4.7 vs 11.4). That pattern fits students who left the course rather than students who scored zero on an exam, so they are excluded. This is an assumption: the dataset cannot prove why these zeros occur. After cleaning, 265 students passed (74.2%) and 92 failed (25.8%), so a model that always predicts \"pass\" would already be right 74.2% of the time. That is the baseline every model must be compared against."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. Exploratory analysis"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "t2o9MUL4s79e"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.barplot(data=df_clean, x=\"failures\", y=\"pass\", ax=axes[0])\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Pass rate by past failures\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Proportion who passed\")\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.barplot(data=df_clean, x=\"studytime\", y=\"pass\", ax=axes[1])\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Pass rate by study time\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Proportion who passed\")\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.histplot(df_clean[\"absences\"], bins=30, ax=axes[2])\n",
        "axes[2].set_title(\"Absences (right-skewed)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Group sizes explain the wide error bars\n",
        "print(df_clean[\"failures\"].value_counts().sort_index())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iPzxNpNkpFh_",
        "outputId": "58f101e0-7245-4351-ac73-48d59004cb62",
        "colab": {
