    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hoCGyiGOvE4o"
      },
      "source": [
        "**What this shows (single split, 90 test students).**\n",
        "\n",
        "- Both models have accuracy close to the baseline of 0.744 (Logistic Regression 0.733, Random Forest 0.767), so accuracy alone says little.\n",
        "- The confusion matrices show the real difference. Logistic Regression identified 8 of the 23 failing students (recall 0.35). Random Forest identified only 3 (recall 0.13) because it predicts \"pass\" for almost everyone. A baseline would identify none.\n",
        "- Random Forest has a slightly higher ROC-AUC (0.668 vs 0.648), but with only 90 test students, a difference of one or two students can change these numbers. A single split is not enough to rank the models, which is why cross-validation follows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED)\n",
        "\n",
        "scoring = {\n",
        "    \"accuracy\": \"accuracy\",\n",
        "    \"balanced_acc\": \"balanced_accuracy\",\n",
        "    \"roc_auc\": \"roc_auc\",\n",
        "    \"fail_recall\": make_scorer(recall_score, pos_label=0),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "models = {\n",
        "    \"Baseline\": DummyClassifier(strategy=\"most_frequent\"),\n",
        "    \"LogReg\": make_logreg(),\n",
        "    \"RandomForest\": make_rf(),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "rows = []\n",
        "for name, model in models.items():\n",
        "    scores = cross_validate(model, X, y, cv=cv, scoring=scoring)\n",
        "    row = {\"model\": name}\n",
        "    for metric in scoring:\n",
        "        vals = scores[f\"test_{metric}\"]\n",
        "        row[metric] = f\"{vals.mean():.3f} +/- {vals.std():.3f}\"\n",
        "    rows.append(row)\n",
        "\n",
        "cv_results = pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"model\")\n",
        "cv_results"
      ],
