        "id": "Zu5g-HnBvE4t"
      },
      "source": [
        "**What this shows (permutation importance on the 90-student test set).**\n",
        "\n",
        "- In the primary analysis, `failures`, `absences`, `schoolsup` and `goout` are the features that matter most, for both models in different degrees. `failures` and `absences` have a clear effect in both models; `schoolsup` and `goout` are clearer for Logistic Regression than for Random Forest.\n",
        "- Features lower in the plot (`Mjob`, `age`, `health`, `studytime`) have error bars that cross zero, especially for Random Forest, so they should not be called important.\n",
        "- Error bars are large because the test set is small, so the order within the top four could change with another split.\n",
        "\n",
        "The main claim is therefore modest: in the primary analysis, **past failures, absences, extra school support and going out were the most consistently important features across methods** (coefficient stability and permutation importance for two different models). The sensitivity analysis in Section 8 shows that only `failures` and `schoolsup` stay on top when the zero-grade students are kept. All of these are associations, not causes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6CzVF7ScI3Pf"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 8. Sensitivity analysis: keeping the G3 = 0 students\n",
        "\n",
        "To test whether excluding the 38 students with G3 = 0 drives the conclusions, the same pipeline and 5-fold cross-validation were run on all 395 students, counting G3 = 0 as a fail. Accuracy is not comparable across the two populations because the baseline changes (0.742 vs 0.671), so balanced accuracy, ROC-AUC and fail recall are compared instead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Sensitivity analysis: include all 395 records\n",
        "df_all = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Treat G3 = 0 as failing, and G3 >= 10 as passing\n",
        "df_all[\"pass\"] = (df_all[\"G3\"] >= 10).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Exclude earlier grades and target from predictors\n",
        "X_all = df_all.drop(columns=[\"G1\", \"G2\", \"G3\", \"pass\"])\n",
        "y_all = df_all[\"pass\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Reuse the same cross-validation strategy and model definitions\n",
        "rows_all = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for name, model in models.items():\n",
        "    scores = cross_validate(\n",
        "        model, X_all, y_all,\n",
        "        cv=cv,\n",
        "        scoring=scoring\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    row = {\"model\": name}\n",
        "    for metric in scoring:\n",
        "        vals = scores[f\"test_{metric}\"]\n",
        "        row[metric] = f\"{vals.mean():.3f} +/- {vals.std():.3f}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    rows_all.append(row)\n",
        "\n",
        "cv_results_all = pd.DataFrame(rows_all).set_index(\"model\")\n",
        "cv_results_all"
      ],
