        "id": "btf3VwFiI3Pg"
      },
      "source": [
        "**What this shows.**\n",
        "\n",
        "- **The main finding holds.** On both populations, ROC-AUC is about 0.68 to 0.72, so the signal is weak but real.\n",
        "- **The model ranking is not stable.** Logistic Regression had the higher ROC-AUC on the primary population (0.717 vs 0.669) and Random Forest on all 395 students (0.702 vs 0.682). Both gaps are within the fold-to-fold spread, so neither model can be called better.\n",
        "- **Random Forest benefits most from the extra fail cases.** Its fail recall rises from 0.05 to 0.22. Failing students make up 32.9% of the data instead of 25.8%, so the forest predicts \"fail\" more often at the default 0.5 threshold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Permutation importance on the sensitivity population (all 395 students)\n",
        "Xa_train, Xa_test, ya_train, ya_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X_all, y_all, test_size=0.25, stratify=y_all, random_state=SEED\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "lr_all = make_logreg().fit(Xa_train, ya_train)\n",
        "rf_all = make_rf().fit(Xa_train, ya_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "def perm_table_for(model, X_te, y_te, name):\n",
        "    r = permutation_importance(\n",
        "        model, X_te, y_te, scoring=\"roc_auc\", n_repeats=30, random_state=SEED\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "        \"feature\": X_te.columns,\n",
        "        f\"{name}_mean\": r.importances_mean,\n",
        "        f\"{name}_std\": r.importances_std,\n",
        "    }).set_index(\"feature\")\n",
        "\n",
        "importance_all = (\n",
        "    perm_table_for(lr_all, Xa_test, ya_test, \"LR\")\n",
        "    .join(perm_table_for(rf_all, Xa_test, ya_test, \"RF\"))\n",
        ")\n",
        "importance_all[\"avg\"] = importance_all[[\"LR_mean\", \"RF_mean\"]].mean(axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Rank of each feature in the primary analysis vs the sensitivity analysis\n",
        "importance[\"avg\"] = importance[[\"LR_mean\", \"RF_mean\"]].mean(axis=1)\n",
        "rank_table = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"avg_sensitivity\": importance_all[\"avg\"],\n",
        "    \"rank_sensitivity\": importance_all[\"avg\"].rank(ascending=False).astype(int),\n",
        "    \"rank_primary\": importance[\"avg\"].rank(ascending=False).astype(int),\n",
        "})\n",
        "rank_table.sort_values(\"rank_sensitivity\").head(8).round(3)"
      ],
