      "source": [
        "**Feature importance across populations.** `failures` is the top feature in both analyses and `schoolsup` is in the top three in both. `absences` and `goout` lose importance when the zero-grade students are kept. A possible reason is that these students all have 0 recorded absences yet are counted as failing, which weakens the usual relationship between absences and failing, but this was not tested. Features below the top three have importance close to zero and their rank changes between analyses, so they should not be interpreted."
