        "## 9. Probability calibration\n",
        "\n",
        "Probability calibration was evaluated using out-of-fold predicted probabilities generated through five-fold stratified cross-validation. The Brier scores were 0.177 for Logistic Regression, 0.179 for Random Forest, and 0.191 for a baseline model that predicted the overall pass rate for every student.\n",
        "\n",
        "Both machine-learning models achieved lower Brier scores than the baseline, with Logistic Regression performing marginally better. The calibration plots showed that predicted probabilities were reasonably close to observed pass rates in several probability bins, although deviations from perfect calibration remained.\n",
        "\n",
        "These findings suggest that the models provide some useful probabilistic information, but their predictions should not be treated as fully reliable individual-level estimates. The Brier score also reflects discrimination as well as calibration, and the limited sample size makes the calibration curves approximate."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Jd_PcBdjkVcK"
